From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:28:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: add SwissPPNFTL checkpoint encoding and GC planning

Preserve the recovered whole-device map and opaque checkpoint payloads in bounded snapshots. Encode native context metadata and range fragments, then validate relocation, checkpoint readback and cold-recovery receipts through an offline GC transaction.

Keep media erase disconnected while native accounting, VFL bank rotation and the 64 GB erase granule remain unqualified. The driver-api note records these limits and the next protocol work.

Validation: 17 recovery and reclamation cases under host ASan/UBSan, 24 metadata records compared with the pinned native formatter, and 209 checkpoint map roundtrips through the Python decoder. Kernel compilation and physical qualification remain pending.

Assisted-by: LLM
